{"id": "20509416", "revid": "20010306", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20509416", "title": "Western Canary Islands goldcrest", "text": "The Western Canary Islands goldcrest (Regulus regulus ellenthalerae) is a subspecies of the goldcrest. It is restricted to the western Canary Islands of La Palma and El Hierro where it is a non-migratory resident.\nPreviously thought to be the same taxon as the Tenerife Goldcrest (\"Regulus regulus teneriffae\"), it was separated as a distinct subspecies of the goldcrest which apparently evolved from an independent colonisation of the islands 1.3\u20131.8 million years ago."}
